<title>SPAIN: Iberia signs separate deals with AA, BA.</title>
<headline>Iberia signs separate deals with AA, BA.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1997-07-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Spanish flagship carrier Iberiahas signed separate commercial deals with U.S.-based American Airlines and British Airways, said state holding group Sociedad Estatal de Participaciones Industriales (SEPI) on Friday.</p>
<p>Both non-Spanish carriers have an option to buy a minority stake in Iberia up until December 31, SEPI said in a statement. These purchases would kick off state-owned Iberia's privatisation, the statement said.</p>
<p>In addition, American will buy 10 percent of Aerolineas Argentinas. Iberia will retain 10 percent of the Argentine airline it controls while the remainder will be sold, the statement said.</p>
</text>
